## Web: choosing a photo reaches the checklist and Guard fails closed
/scan -> "Pumili ng isang larawan mula sa gallery" (_method: page file input injected with the repo fixture
dev-assets/model-fixtures/v1-rust.jpg, served by the dev server at /assets/?unstable_path=...).
Result: routed to /symptom-checklist with "Checking your photo…" and
  "The sugarcane photo check is not available on this phone, so scans are paused. Update or reinstall the app, then try again."
Selecting the "Raised rust-colored …" symptom afterwards leaves "Continue to analysis result" disabled
  (state stays paused; no analysis screen is reachable).
evidence: web-guard-fail-closed.png (this round), r3-web-03-guard-unavailable-fail-closed.png (round 3)

## Device recheck after an adb server hang
The Windows-side adb server that exposes the USB phone had hung (client connects, no response). The two hung
adb processes were stopped by exact PID and the server was restarted with the Windows platform-tools adb.
After restart: `adb devices -l` -> AYAUFIN76LEYR46X device product:duchamp_global model:2311DRK48G.
Installed app: com.niks0501.caneguard versionName=2.2.1 (lastUpdateTime 2026-11-15 00:22:44).
`npm run start:dev-client -- --port 8081` + `adb reverse tcp:8081` + `adb reverse tcp:8210` reused the installed
dev client over Metro (no native delta in this change, so the runbook's reuse path applies; a local gradlew build is
not possible here: Android platform-tools only, no gradle/sdkmanager, no android/ project).
Fresh screenshot of the live app on that bundle: r4-device-00-current.png (scan result screen from the round-3
acceptance sequence, same revision).

## Phone scenarios (driven in round 3 of this same pipeline run, revision a9c22b5)
Recorded in r3-live-acceptance.log with screenshots r3-device-0*.png and persisted-state dumps r3-caneguard-*.db:
- gallery sugarcane photo -> Guard accepts -> five-label V2 result (smut 0.9823, rssi 0.0142, rust 0.0018,
  healthy 0.0017, mosaic 0.0001 in scan_class_scores)
- gallery non-sugarcane photo -> "This does not look like sugarcane", Continue absent, scan_records unchanged (0)
- airplane mode repeat: accept still yields a result, reject still shows the retake message, no new record
- EXIF-rotated portrait accepted (orientation applied; oracle 0.979 upright vs 0.259 without EXIF)
- per-scan latency/memory recorded from scan_records (inference_ms 113.0/150.6, total_ms 395.1/758.2)

## Not drivable
- Camera capture: the device viewfinder renders an all-black (rear) / near-black (front) frame in this setup, so a
  camera-originated photo fails the photo-quality gate ("The image has low contrast"). Gallery capture on the same
  device is the substitute path and is what the accept/reject scenarios used.
